recorded 2026-11-12 9.0.10 neutralized
The T050 spike (research.md "9.0 webservice spike (D-23 step 2, T050, 2026-11-12 UTC)") on a non-production 9.0.10 server without a cluster, D-2 steps 1-4 in the REST_90 variant: loginUserCli ok, getNode ok with a non-empty node name, clusterDownload of webservice.log without exception, the downloaded file at the requested path with 0 bytes, exit 0. Before login the REST client printed one stdout line outside any frame, in log4j's status-logger form "<ISO-8601 timestamp> main ERROR Unable to load io.netty.resolver.dns.macos.MacOSDnsServerAddressStreamProvider, fallback to system defaults. ...".
Inferred, not recorded: the throwaway program printed its steps, not helper frames, so empty.frames is written in the helper protocol (D-4, D-5) from that outcome: start REST_90, login ok, node ok, part log ok 0 (D-8: a present 0-byte log), end, with the fixed nonce; the recorded node name is replaced by node1. The netty line after start is the one taken over from the recorded fixtures/queue-entry/v9_0/not_found_file.frames (9.0.10), whose shape the T050 line has; its timestamp is not the T050 one. empty.log is the 0-byte file, so no log content was neutralized.
